	(text "Notes:\n- External IO is individual through-hole solder pads: each wire is stripped and\n  soldered once, it is never crimped. Every pad carries its own silkscreen label,\n  taken from its VALUE field. J7 is the only connector.\n- TX/RX are BOARD-side names: the pad named TX carries the board's UART*_TX net.\n  Check against the mark1 cables before soldering.\n- CON-1 (J10-J13) and CON-3 (J30-J33) carry the same four signals; CON-3 may stay\n  unwired (SRC-3) until a real radio arrives.\n- The I2C1 pull-ups live on the Sensors sheet, so there are none here.\n- The ESC has TWO parallel paths onto the same nets: the J40-J48 pads and the J7\n  connector. J7 is a JST-SH 1.00 mm receptacle that mates with the plug already\n  fitted to the T-Motor Velox 45A V2 harness, so that harness plugs straight in,\n  stays removable and needs no soldering. The J6 pads are the brand-agnostic path\n  for any other 4-in-1 ESC, and the path that survives vibration: the SH has no\n  lock. Connector for the bench, pads for flight. Every other interface is pads\n  only - CON-1, CON-2 and CON-3 get no connector.\n- ################ ONLY J7 HAS A PIN NUMBERING ################\n  Since 2026-08-17 the ESC pads are individual pads (J40-J48), so there is no\n  second pad ORDER to get wrong: each pad states its signal on the silkscreen,\n  on both faces. This removed what used to be the most likely wiring mistake on\n  this board, the ESC-3 spec order versus the Velox order.\n  J7 keeps a numbering, the MEASURED Velox wire order (2026-08-16):\n      1 GND, 2 GND, 3 VBAT, 4 10V, 5 M4, 6 M3, 7 M2, 8 M1, 9 CURR, 10 TLM\n  Note the motor order runs backwards there. Placement of J40-J48 may follow\n  that same order so pads and connector read alike.\n  4-in-1 pin orders are not standard across brands, so any hand-made harness\n  must still be checked wire by wire with a continuity check before power-up.\n  #############################################################\n- J41 and J7 carry the BOARD'S MAIN POWER INPUT: +10V from the ESC BEC (PWR-1).\n  Raw VBAT feeds the PWR-4 divider on the Power sheet, nothing else.\n- The board MUST NOT be fed from raw VBAT: motor braking spikes on a 6S pack can\n  exceed the AP63205 32 V input rating, and the ESC BEC absorbs them.\n- CURR is the analog current-sense fallback (PWR-4 / SRC-3); TLM is the ESC\n  telemetry UART RX (ESC-2). USART2_TX has no pad, only the TP5 test point.\n- Pads are placed one by one, wherever they fit, with a silkscreen label each\n  (MEC-5): external IO no longer reserves a fixed length of board edge, and a\n  second row is usable because the holes are plated and labelled on both faces.\n  The SWD header and the USB-C receptacle share one board edge facing a lateral\n  side of the drone (MEC-2).\n- All hierarchical nets leave this sheet to the MCU sheet; nothing is wired between\n  sheet blocks in the root."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "289820ca-80f8-4b66-9b9a-16b630046e45")
	)
	(text "J7 - ESC connector for the T-Motor Velox 45A V2 harness (MEASURED WIRE order, NOT the J6 order)\n1 GND, 2 GND, 3 VBAT, 4 10V, 5 M4, 6 M3, 7 M2, 8 M1, 9 CURR, 10 TLM"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "db7ad83d-411f-445e-8c48-c4258a50e0e6")
	)
	(text "CON-1 telemetry UART (USART1), 4 pads: J10 GND, J11 5V, J12 RX1, J13 TX1"
